SRC/eff_lp -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  lpq.c    the job table's printer test passed strcmp() one CHARACTER of           the printer's name, queue->printer[n][0], where the name itself           belongs -- K&R C has no prototype to catch it.  strcmp then read           a string at the character's value as an address, low memory, so           whether a job was listed depended on what that memory held:           with zeros there every job was skipped and lpq said `No           Spooljobs' over a queue it had just counted.  The [0] is gone.           Found by the os9exec session, 2026-09-25.  The original is           lpq.c.ori.